# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Audiobook Creation Tool — .gitignore
#  Auto-generated / machine-specific artifacts that must never be committed.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Virtual environment (repo root; rebuilt fresh by Setup_and_Run on each machine)
.venv/
# Isolated Qwen3-TTS environment (created by the in-app "Install / repair Qwen3 voices" action; never committed or packaged).
# Since v0.7.0 P04C it is created inside .venv (.venv/engines/qwen3, covered above); the older location beside it:
.venv-qwen3/
# Isolated OmniVoice environment (v0.8.0). Owner decision 2026-11-13 (unified .venv layout): it is created inside
# .venv (.venv/engines/omnivoice, covered above), beside Qwen3's. The earlier location beside .venv is never used again;
# it stays ignored so a copy that still has one can never commit or package it (shared/release.py also excludes every
# .venv-* folder). Its wheels, model, receipts and set-aside folder live in files/runtime-data/.
.venv-omnivoice/
# The bootstrap's own set-aside environments during a repair (.venv.replaced, .venv.replaced-<n>, .venv.discarded…).
# They can hold the Qwen3 engine while it is carried across; never committed or packaged.
/.venv.replaced*/
/.venv.discarded*/
.python_runtime/

# Python bytecode / caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/

# Build / packaging artifacts
dist/
build/
*.spec
*.egg-info/

# Portable binaries (ffmpeg, etc.) — downloaded by the bootstrap
files/bin/

# Runtime-writable state: logs, settings.json, and the HuggingFace model
# cache (~300 MB Kokoro weights, kept in-tree but never committed).
# Delete files/runtime-data/ + files/bin/ + .venv/ for a full "uninstall".
files/runtime-data/

# Owner preservation of the pre-fresh-install HOME-PC state (v0.7.0 plan §3, tag
# 20261021-184021-592ae0be). Exact, root-anchored directory names only: these hold
# private environments and runtime data and are never staged, packaged or cleaned.
/.venv.act67-preserved-20261021-184021-592ae0be/
/.venv-qwen3.act67-preserved-20261021-184021-592ae0be/
/files/runtime-data.act67-preserved-20261021-184021-592ae0be/

# Test logs / harness outputs (any folder named test-logs, at any depth)
test-logs/

# Per-voice manual-listen QA samples (generated by tts/generate_voice_samples.py)
files/test-for-manual-listen-elmatthe/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# files/test-files/  — entirely untracked.
# LOCAL testing fixtures only (PDFs, MP3s, M4Bs, EPUBs — may include
# copyrighted media); nothing under it is ever staged or committed.
# To use a fixture in code, point at it via an env var (e.g.
# KOKORO_TEST_PDF_FOLDER) or an absolute path — never rely on git.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
files/test-files/
test-files/

# Voice-timing test corpus (copyrighted light-novel PDFs + rendered audio) —
# same rule as files/test-files/: local fixtures only, never staged.
files/livid-lady-test-files/

# Bundled clone references (v0.8.0, owner decision 2026-11-13): each cloned engine has
# its own folder and its own six WAVs, and only those 18, by exact name, are tracked.
# Git cannot re-include a file inside an ignored folder, so each engine folder is
# re-included first and then everything in it is ignored again except its six WAVs.
# Anything else placed anywhere under Cloned-Voice-Uploads/ (loose files at its root,
# other folders, copies, notes, MP3s) stays local. Derivatives/caches use runtime-data/.
files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/*
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Chatterbox/
files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Chatterbox/*
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Chatterbox/Chatterbox - Female 1.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Chatterbox/Chatterbox - Female 2.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Chatterbox/Chatterbox - Male 1.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Chatterbox/Chatterbox - Male 2.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Chatterbox/Chatterbox - Male 3.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Chatterbox/Chatterbox - Male 4.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/OmniVoice/
files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/OmniVoice/*
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/OmniVoice/OmniVoice - Female 1.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/OmniVoice/OmniVoice - Female 2.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/OmniVoice/OmniVoice - Male 1.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/OmniVoice/OmniVoice - Male 2.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/OmniVoice/OmniVoice - Male 3.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/OmniVoice/OmniVoice - Male 4.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Qwen3/
files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Qwen3/*
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Qwen3/Qwen3 - Female 1.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Qwen3/Qwen3 - Female 2.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Qwen3/Qwen3 - Male 1.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Qwen3/Qwen3 - Male 2.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Qwen3/Qwen3 - Male 3.wav
!files/Cloned-Voice-Uploads/Qwen3/Qwen3 - Male 4.wav
# The pre-v0.7.0 reference folder: the app no longer reads it. It keeps only the
# owner's curated MP3 source recordings (read-only, local-only) — ignored whole, so
# a WAV can never be re-added at the old path.
files/Chatterbox-Voice-Uploads/

# Agent config (.claude/, .codex/) — local per-machine wiring, removed from tracking
# 2026-07-08 (d3443fe / e7cecd1); intentionally never tracked. Local copies stay on disk.
.claude/
.codex/

# AI-WORKSPACE.md — private local reference (machine conventions incl. the HOME-MacOS
# section); intentionally never tracked. The local copy stays on disk as-is.
AI-WORKSPACE.md
REPO-STRUCTURE.md

# vibe-coding-templates — permanently removed reference material; do not track or restore.
files/vibe-coding-templates/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor / IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Windows Batch Files
Map-Repo-Structure.bat

# Local developer workspace (v0.6.2 Plan 5, 2026-08-29 maintainer policy).
# All agent/developer scratch, diagnostics, synthetic fixtures, generated media,
# backups, clean-room copies and temporary evidence live here instead of in
# external folders. Do not create project workspaces outside the repository.
# Deliberate cross-platform fixtures stay in their approved tracked paths.
# v0.7.2: the verification gate and the feature map are tracked source inside it; each gate run's outputs are not.
# A directory rule (files/dev-work/) would make these exceptions dead: git never looks inside an excluded directory.
files/dev-work/*
!files/dev-work/verification-gate/
files/dev-work/verification-gate/outputs/
!files/dev-work/feature-map/

# Maintainer archives: local-only, never tracked, packaged or published.
files/Archives/

# Setup downloads (stage 0 keeps the verified Python installer here until Python is proven).
files/temp/
